From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:40:44 +0000
Subject: Show page info from the address bar

Chromium 158 moves page info into the app menu ("Site controls") on
phones (AndroidPageInfoAsAppMenuItem, on by default). With it, secure
pages show no icon at the start of the address bar, and the icon shown
on other pages, including the browser's own pages, does nothing when
tapped.

Keep page info on the address bar: the status icon shows the page's
security state again and opens page info when tapped, as before the
move. Site controls stays in the app menu, where the menu with the
back button (ThreeDotMenuBackButton) lists it as well.

